usage: run_benchmark_categories.py [-h] [--python PYTHON]
                                   [--output-dir OUTPUT_DIR]
                                   [--duration DURATION] [--warmup WARMUP]
                                   [--concurrency CONCURRENCY]
                                   [--repetitions REPETITIONS] [--seed SEED]
                                   [--category-timeout CATEGORY_TIMEOUT]
                                   [--expected-source-sha256 EXPECTED_SOURCE_SHA256]
                                   [--expected-native-sha256 EXPECTED_NATIVE_SHA256]
                                   [--expected-public-cases EXPECTED_PUBLIC_CASES]
                                   [--capture-identity CAPTURE_IDENTITY]
                                   [--parity-before-identity PARITY_BEFORE_IDENTITY]
                                   [--parity-report PARITY_REPORT]
                                   [--skip-analysis]

Run the maintained ASGI benchmark categories against stock live references.
Build the normal server and Rust clients before invoking this wrapper. Capture
an identity, run the complete public parity suite on that binary, then supply
both artifacts. Every category runs sequentially and retains its original
JSON, JSONL, server logs, and failure observations. No package is published.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --python PYTHON       checkout .venv/bin/python used by every maintained
                        category
  --output-dir OUTPUT_DIR
  --duration DURATION
  --warmup WARMUP
  --concurrency CONCURRENCY
  --repetitions REPETITIONS
  --seed SEED
  --category-timeout CATEGORY_TIMEOUT
  --expected-source-sha256 EXPECTED_SOURCE_SHA256
  --expected-native-sha256 EXPECTED_NATIVE_SHA256
  --expected-public-cases EXPECTED_PUBLIC_CASES
  --capture-identity CAPTURE_IDENTITY
                        capture normal prebuilt identities before public
                        parity; runs no benchmarks
  --parity-before-identity PARITY_BEFORE_IDENTITY
  --parity-report PARITY_REPORT
  --skip-analysis       retain only category artifacts; default runs the pure-
                        JSON analyzer
